th retained match indexes only for surviving voters','A2':'Latest configuration determines campaign targets and eligibility'})\nb('b-consume','A5','Main loop processLogs and serialized FSM goroutine','Log index/term/type and FSM dispatch/completion boundary','Leader commit notification or follower commit bound',['src-application-dispatch','src-fsm-consumer','src-fsm-rest','src-fsm-contract'],consumes_fact_ids=['f-commit-bound'],writes=['processLogs reads entries up to bound, prepares command/barrier/config tuples, enqueues batches and advances dispatch lastApplied','FSM invokes Apply or ApplyBatch and responds to associated futures after return'],important_branches=['No-op is not sent to FSM; barriers complete on FSM thread; configuration handling varies by protocol/FSM interface','Snapshot restore is serialized with apply by fsmMutateCh'],async_boundaries=['Enqueued/lastApplied is not completed FSM.Apply'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'ApplyFuture completion reports the associated FSM response'})\nb('b-recovery','A3','NewRaft initialization, main snapshot RPC handler and FSM worker','Snapshot index/term/configuration and stored suffix','Startup or InstallSnapshot',['src-startup','src-install','src-snapshot-send','src-fsm-rest'],writes=['Startup loads current term and last log, restores first usable snapshot, then scans later configuration entries','InstallSnapshot checks term/version/size, persists snapshot, waits for FSM restoration, sets applied/snapshot positions and both configurations'],important_branches=['Install compaction failures logged after restore; monotonic stores remove old logs','NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart skips FSM restore but adopts snapshot metadata'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Successful snapshot acknowledgement contributes match index','A2':'Recovered history and configuration constrain later election and replication'})\nb('b-persistence','A6','Main term/vote paths, snapshot worker and storage implementations','Durable term, vote, log and snapshot metadata','Term/vote update, snapshot request or bootstrap',['src-durable-term-vote','src-snapshot-create','src-bootstrap'],durable_effects=['Term failure panics; grant follows both vote writes','Bootstrap requires no prior state and writes term 1 configuration','Snapshot pairs completed FSM position with committed configuration at or below it, persists then compacts'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Persisted vote and log freshness carry context across restart'})\nb('b-client','A7','API caller, main loop and futures','Operation future identity and leader tenure','Apply/Barrier and user restore',['src-client-apply','src-user-restore','src-leader-loop-rest'],writes=['Apply timeout bounds enqueue; admitted future waits for response','User restore rejects outstanding configuration change, aborts inflight requests, burns a fresh index, restores FSM using current configuration and updates snapshot/log metadata'],important_branches=['ErrLeadershipLost does not promise absence of effects'],cross_activity_effects={'A3':'Restore creates log discontinuity that forces lagging followers toward snapshot installation'})\nb('b-verify','A2','Main loop verifyLeader, follower notifyAll and verifyFuture mutex','Verification future and latest voter-count threshold','VerifyLeader request triggers immediate heartbeat notifications',['src-leader-loop-rest','src-repl-owner','src-verify-tally','src-heartbeat','src-transfer-lease'],writes=['Starts at one self vote and threshold quorumSize; registers future on all replication workers','notifyAll passes success boolean to tally; threshold or negative vote wakes main loop'],important_branches=['Leader lease separately counts recent contact only from Voters','Verification success completes future; negative vote triggers follower transition'],unknowns=['Can acknowledgements from Nonvoter workers satisfy verification despite absence of voter quorum?'])\nF=[dict(id='f-match',meaning='The tenure-local commitment map records a monotonically increasing acknowledged log index for each currently included voter. Local storage completion, successful append replies with entries, and successful snapshot replies are distinct establishment paths.',identity={'tenure':'commitment object','participant':'ServerID'},validity_context='Only configured voter keys participate; new leader creates a new map. Configuration replacement retains indexes of surviving voter IDs.',representation=['commitment.matchIndexes'],durability='Volatile accounting over durable log/snapshot effects; acknowledgements themselves are not persisted.',recovery='New tenure starts zero match indexes and reconstructs them through local dispatch and replication.',source_ids=['src-commitment','src-dispatch-config','src-replication-accounting','src-snapshot-send'],invalidators=['b-leader-context'],reinterpreters=['b-configuration'],unknowns=[]),dict(id='f-commit-bound',meaning='The local commitIndex is the implementation-selected upper index for committed-log dispatch. Leader sets it from current-tenure quorum accounting; follower sets it from min(received leader commit, local last index). This fact records the selected bound, not proof that every local entry through it matches the leader.',identity={'replica':'Raft instance','position':'log index with local term/content'},validity_context='Normal leader/follower append processing; follower selection follows term/predecessor checks and any replacement performed for this request. processLogs separately suppresses indexes already dispatched.',representation=['raftState.commitIndex','AppendEntriesRequest.LeaderCommitIndex'],durability='Commit index is in-memory; log and snapshots supply persisted history.',recovery='Startup reconstructs log/snapshot context; subsequent leader/follower processing learns commitment.',source_ids=['src-leader-consume','src-follower-append','src-application-dispatch','src-startup'],unknowns=['Relationship between a limited request matched prefix and a longer retained local suffix needs investigation.'])]\nacts=[]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nfor a,r in roles.items():\n bs=[x for x in B if x['primary_activity']==a]\n acts.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=r['relation'],realization_summary='; '.join(x['trigger'] for x in bs),entry_points=[x['execution_owner'] for x in bs],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(y for x in bs for y in x['source_ids']))))\ndef path(t,bs,fs,ss):return dict(explanation=t,behavior_ids=bs,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=ss)\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured HashiCorp Raft Go package: library owns election, replication, membership, recovery and asynchronous FSM dispatch. Callers provide deterministic FSM and storage/transport implementations; in-repository implementations remain within the investigation boundary.',protocol_contexts=['Leader terms, latest/committed configurations, log and snapshot index/term'],external_interfaces=['Raft.Apply/Barrier/VerifyLeader, membership and snapshot APIs','Transport, LogStore, StableStore, SnapshotStore, FSM'],ownership=['Main Raft loop, per-peer replication/heartbeat workers, serialized FSM worker, snapshot worker'],variants=['Protocol compatibility modes, pre-vote support, batching FSM, monotonic log storage'],source_ids=['src-startup','src-fsm-contract','src-suffrage-contract']),activities=acts,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries commit bound',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-follower-append'],reason='Does limited-batch catch-up authorize consumption beyond the matched prefix?',source_ids=['src-follower-append','src-pipeline-and-batches'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries StoreLogs failure after truncation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-follower-append'],reason='Determine fault contract and stale cached lastLog consumers.',source_ids=['src-follower-append'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.verifyLeader',disposition='mapped',beha